Organisation:- 	It help you to do is manage multiple aws accounts. 

Service control policies:- It restrice what account can do. applied to SA and individual unit.
With aws organisation you can actually limit what an aws account can actually do using a feature called service control policies
It is like Iam policies but at the account level.
You can restrict what an account can actually do. So you can apply service control policies that allow the account to work with certain services and not with other services. 

Organizational Unit:- Allow you to group accounts with similar business or security requirements.
It is used when you have to manage the multiple aws accounts. It acts like an parant container for similarly configured aws accounts. You can apply a service control policy to the organizational unit and all the accounts whithin that organizational unit will then inharit the same service pollicy. 

 
